IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`

-- INSTRUMENT: Singapore Broadcasting Authority (Class Licence) (Amendment) Notification 2001 (S 496/2001), made under ss 21 and 23 of the Singapore Broadcasting Authority Act (Cap. 297).
-- Deposit: ../../../singapore-broadcasting-authority-class-licence-amendment-notification-2001/registers/source-bundle/BA1994-S496-2001.txt (e-Gazette PDF, pdftotext -layout, unedited). Quotations below are lines of THAT file; `srcrefs.py` is run on this module against it.
-- First published 8 October 2001 at 5:00 pm; "shall come into operation on 10th October 2001" (paragraph 1).
-- It amends the Schedule to the Class Licence Notification (N 1) as it stood under the Singapore Broadcasting Authority Act (new paragraph 2A, paragraph 3(a) deleted, paragraphs 5 and 6 amended). The Schedule is not in the lawplain text of N 1.

§ `Paragraph 2: the Schedule amended`

-- src:3 | First published in the Government Gazette, Electronic Edition, on 8th October 2001 at 5:00 pm.
-- src:21 | 1. This Notification may be cited as the Singapore Broadcasting
-- src:22 | Authority (Class Licence) (Amendment) Notification 2001 and
-- src:23 | shall come into operation on 10th October 2001.
@ref S 496/2001 publication line and para 1 (commencement) (src:3-23)
GIVEN `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 496/2001 the amendments are in operation on` MEANS
    `the day of the conduct` AT LEAST (Date 10 10 2001)

-- src:28 | (a) by inserting, immediately after paragraph 2, the following
-- src:29 | paragraph:
-- src:30 | ‘‘2A.—(1) Subject to sub-paragraph (2), an Internet Content
-- src:31 | Provider who is or is determined by the Authority to be a political
-- src:32 | party registered in Singapore providing any programme on the
-- src:33 | World Wide Web through the Internet shall —
-- src:34 | (a) in the case of an Internet Content Provider who was
-- src:35 | registered with the Authority under the provisions of this
-- src:36 | Notification in force before 10th October 2001, re-register
-- src:37 | with the Authority within 14 days of that date; or
-- src:38 | (b) in any other case, register with the Authority within 14 days
-- src:39 | of the commencement of its service.
-- src:40 | (2) Notwithstanding sub-paragraph (1), the Authority may permit
-- src:41 | the Internet Content Provider to register or re-register, as the case
-- src:42 | may be, with the Authority within such longer time as the Authority
-- src:43 | may permit.’’;
@ref S 496/2001 para 2(a): Schedule para 2A (a political party Internet Content Provider registers or re-registers within 14 days) (src:28-43)
GIVEN `the provider is, or is determined by the Authority to be, a political party registered in Singapore providing a programme on the World Wide Web through the Internet` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider was registered under the Notification in force before 10 October 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days from 10 October 2001, or from the commencement of the service if later, to the registration` IS A NUMBER
      `the Authority permitted a longer time and the registration was within it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 496/2001 N 1 Schedule para 2A the provider has registered or re-registered in time` MEANS
    (NOT `the provider is, or is determined by the Authority to be, a political party registered in Singapore providing a programme on the World Wide Web through the Internet`) OR `the number of days from 10 October 2001, or from the commencement of the service if later, to the registration` AT MOST 14 OR `the Authority permitted a longer time and the registration was within it`

-- S 496/2001 para 2(b) (deposit line 45) deletes sub-paragraph (a) of Schedule para 3: a deletion; no rule.

-- src:48 | (c) by deleting paragraph 5 and substituting the following
-- src:49 | paragraph:
-- src:50 | ‘‘5. An Internet Content Provider who is required to register or
-- src:51 | re-register, as the case may be, under paragraph 2A, 3 or 4 shall —
-- src:52 | (a) register or re-register in such form and manner as the
-- src:53 | Authority may determine; and
-- src:54 | (b) provide the Authority with such particulars and undertakings
-- src:55 | as the Authority may require in connection with the
-- src:56 | provision of the Internet Content Provider’s service.’’; and
@ref S 496/2001 para 2(c): Schedule para 5 substituted (src:48-56)
GIVEN `the provider registered or re-registered in the form and manner the Authority determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider gave the Authority the particulars and undertakings it required in connection with the provision of the service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 496/2001 N 1 Schedule para 5 the provider has complied` MEANS
    `the provider registered or re-registered in the form and manner the Authority determined` AND `the provider gave the Authority the particulars and undertakings it required in connection with the provision of the service`

-- S 496/2001 para 2(d) (deposit lines 58-61) amends Schedule para 6 to read "register or re-register, as the case may be, under paragraph 2, 2A, 3 or 4": a wording change to a paragraph the lawplain text does not serve; no rule is stated here.
